  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Deployment target, not a runtime inventory",
      "items": [
        "API and worker share application code: Inventory, Investigation and Security are modules, not independent services.",
        "Postgres and worker placement are target design; their manifests arrive with consuming increments.",
        "Postgres stores relationships and leased jobs; no broker, vector store or graph database."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Identity and connections",
      "items": [
        "Collector, agent, token refresher and observer identities are separate. Credentials remain mounted server-side.",
        "MCP proxy forwards over localhost HTTP to the upstream MCP container; its server identity performs scoped reads.",
        "API and worker use the configured model adapter for investigation. AWS MCP integration deployment is selected per skill.",
        "Remote exposure requires verified identity and recovery gates; no public ingress is implied."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Optional observability mappings",
      "items": [
        "Prometheus operator reconciles monitors; Prometheus scrapes API, kube-state-metrics and node exporter.",
        "Alloy reads allowlisted node-local logs and receives bounded OTLP; it exports to Loki and Tempo.",
        "Grafana queries Prometheus, Loki and Tempo. Each telemetry store has independent persistent storage.",
        "Observer log access does not authorize agent queries. Telemetry failures never block application requests."
      ]
    }
  ]
